      "description": "<p>New Features (Experimental):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Production stacking (<strong>Queue multiple productions</strong>) When one finishes, the next starts automatically.</li>\n<li><em>Requirements are paid upfront when stacking.</em></li>\n<li><em>Automation only runs while in-game (and not in raid).</em></li>\n<li><em>Tools are only required once for the full production stack.</em></li>\n<li>Automatically moves <strong>produced items to stash</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Stack button</strong> instead of Start button.</li>\n<li>Shows stacked amount and total amount in production.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I started working on this in mid-October. After a lot of tweaking and a complete restart about two weeks ago. I’ve finally made a <strong>playtest-ready version</strong>. It was quite challenging to get everything right while solving multiple issues along the way, so please report any bugs or problems you encounter by creating an issue here: <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://github.com/PMouse23/SPT-HideoutAutomation/issues\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://github.com/PMouse23/SPT-HideoutAutomation/issues</a></p>\n",
